    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0497" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg447"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 199.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Captain T. W. Tucker, commander of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Victoria</hi> on Lake Nicaragua, has applied to me to
                    perform the marriage ceremony for himself and a young lady of this country. Both
                    are Americans and Protestants. Captain Tucker informs me that there is no
                    ordained Protestant minister or other person authorized to conduct a marriage
                    ceremony in Nicaragua other than Catholic clergymen.</p>
                <p>Can you authorize me to perform this ceremony?</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
